        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF142 Animation.commitStyles() automatically fills values]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40585</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40585"/>
        <updated>2025-08-04T01:51:19.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF142 <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Animation/commitStyles" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">Animation/commitStyles()</code></a> allows animations to capture the final styles without specifying a <code class="notranslate">fill</code> in latest spec.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that normally I'd have the new behavior front and center and mention the older behavior as a legacy thing. Unfortunately the advice of the developer is that you can't feature check for this, so people will have to stick with the old behaviour until this is in most browsers.<br>
So this update covers the old case first, and puts the new information second.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3249106813" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40482" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40482/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40482">#40482</a></p>]]></content>
